Lab 9: Integrate Red Hat Quay with RHACM
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Integrate Red Hat Quay with OpenShift clusters for centralized container image management
Configure RHACM to manage container images across multiple clusters
Implement image source control and access policies across distributed environments
Establish secure image distribution workflows using Quay and RHACM
Monitor and manage container image lifecycle across cluster environments
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of OpenShift Container Platform concepts
Familiarity with container images and registries
Knowledge of Kubernetes fundamentals
Experience with YAML configuration files
Understanding of Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management (RHACM) basics
Basic command-line interface (CLI) skills
Lab Environment
Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines: Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines with all necessary tools installed. Simply click Start Lab to begin - no need to build your own virtual machine or install software.

