Task 1: Link Quay to OpenShift Clusters
Subtask 1.1: Verify Lab Environment Setup
First, let's verify that our lab environment is properly configured and accessible.

Access the lab machine terminal

Verify OpenShift cluster connectivity:

# Check cluster status
oc cluster-info

# Verify RHACM installation
oc get pods -n open-cluster-management
Check Quay registry accessibility:
# Test Quay registry connection
curl -k https://quay-registry.apps.cluster.local/health/instance
Subtask 1.2: Configure Quay Integration with OpenShift
Now we'll establish the connection between Quay and our OpenShift clusters.

Create Quay configuration namespace:
# Create dedicated namespace for Quay integration
oc create namespace quay-integration

# Set current context to the new namespace
oc project quay-integration
Create Quay registry secret:
# Create registry authentication secret
oc create secret docker-registry quay-registry-secret \
  --docker-server=quay-registry.apps.cluster.local \
  --docker-username=admin \
  --docker-password=password123 \
  --docker-email=admin@example.com \
  -n quay-integration
Configure image pull secrets globally:
# Link secret to default service account
oc secrets link default quay-registry-secret --for=pull -n quay-integration

# Create cluster-wide image pull secret
oc create secret docker-registry quay-global-secret \
  --docker-server=quay-registry.apps.cluster.local \
  --docker-username=admin \
  --docker-password=password123 \
  --docker-email=admin@example.com \
  -n openshift-config
Subtask 1.3: Create Quay Integration Configuration
Create Quay operator configuration:
cat << 'EOF' > quay-integration-config.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: quay-integration-config
  namespace: quay-integration
data:
  config.yaml: |
    AUTHENTICATION_TYPE: Database
    BUILDLOGS_REDIS:
      host: quay-redis
      port: 6379
    DATABASE_SECRET_KEY: a-random-secret-key
    DB_URI: postgresql://quay:password@quay-database:5432/quay
    DISTRIBUTED_STORAGE_CONFIG:
      default:
        - LocalStorage
        - storage_path: /datastorage/registry
    DISTRIBUTED_STORAGE_DEFAULT_LOCATIONS: []
    DISTRIBUTED_STORAGE_PREFERENCE:
      - default
    FEATURE_GENERAL_OCI_SUPPORT: true
    FEATURE_LISTEN_IP_VERSION: IPv4
    FEATURE_LOG_EXPORT: true
    FEATURE_QUOTA_MANAGEMENT: true
    FEATURE_RATE_LIMITS: true
    FEATURE_REPO_MIRROR: true
    FEATURE_SECURITY_NOTIFICATIONS: true
    FEATURE_SECURITY_SCANNER: true
    FEATURE_STORAGE_REPLICATION: false
    FEATURE_USER_CREATION: true
    FEATURE_USERNAME_CONFIRMATION: true
    LOGS_MODEL: database
    LOGS_MODEL_CONFIG: {}
    PREFERRED_URL_SCHEME: https
    SECRET_KEY: a-random-secret-key
    SECURITY_SCANNER_INDEXING_INTERVAL: 30
    SERVER_HOSTNAME: quay-registry.apps.cluster.local
    SETUP_COMPLETE: true
    TAG_EXPIRATION_OPTIONS:
      - 0s
      - 1d
      - 1w
      - 2w
      - 4w
    TEAM_RESYNC_STALE_TIME: 60m
    TESTING: false
    USE_CDN: false
EOF

oc apply -f quay-integration-config.yaml
Verify configuration deployment:
# Check ConfigMap creation
oc get configmap quay-integration-config -n quay-integration

# Verify configuration content
oc describe configmap quay-integration-config -n quay-integration
Task 2: Manage Container Images Through RHACM
Subtask 2.1: Configure RHACM for Image Management
Create RHACM image management namespace:
# Create namespace for RHACM image policies
oc create namespace rhacm-image-management

# Switch to the new namespace
oc project rhacm-image-management
Create image policy configuration:
cat << 'EOF' > image-policy-config.yaml
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Policy
